                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "If you have played Roads of Rome I or II you know what III is pretty much all about. ROR III is a time management game that centers around repairing/building the Roads of Rome. To start the game there are four modes: Relax, Easy, Normal, Hard. I choose to play on Normal and had a nice challenging game that wasn't too easy and even though a few of the levels were pretty hard it wasn't overly hard. \n\nAs you begin playing you must decide how best to use your workers to gather supplies and build buildings while doing this as quickly as possible. You must gather wood, food, water, gold, stone as well as special items such as gems and rune stones. Several buildings are available to build to help gather the fore mentioned supplies. There are also special buildings and items to build as well. New to ROR III is the appearance of fire on the roads and in buildings, which you must put out with water.\n\nSome of the maps may be familiar from previous games in the series, but most maps are not exact duplicates. To complete the game you have to make your way through 40 levels and if you have completed them all expertly you will open three final levels you can play.\n\nI recommend this game as it is a very good game for the money, for those times you want to just have some easy and good fun.",
